A||N||2||Dan87GT||V6 Starting problems||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||06-09-2000||09:13 AM||||Whenever I first start my 86SE it dies unless I give it gas. If I keep restarting it 10+ times it will finally idle. I have checked the vacuum lines, cap, rotor, plugs, etc, and found no problems. Any thoughts???||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||06-09-2000||10:14 AM||||<BR>You mentioned the regular tune-up stuff, but it sounds like a fuel delivery problem.<P>Have you replaced the fuel filter?<P>Also, can you hear the fuel pump whiring? The fuel pump should whir about 2 seconds. If you replace the fuel pump, replace the fuel strainer that attaches to the fuel pump as well.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||CD||06-09-2000||09:49 PM||||I had the same problem with my 87GT and I replaced many of the parts you mentioned.  I finally ended up replacing a $25 temperature sensor which eliminated the problem.  Your defective temperature sensor may be telling the computer that the engine is hot when it is in fact cold.  Which would explain why it stalls so many times before finally idling.||||reg||1
